sentences.l:
and it, rolling, rang beneath the feet of the horses,
the tubed helm, and were defiled the plumes
with blood and with dust;

before this indeed it was not custom
for the horse-plumed helmet to be defiled with dust,
but the head and the lovely forehead of a divine man
it protected, of Achilles;

And as when a tireless boar a lion overpowered in the joy of battle,
the two who on the peaks of a mountain, greatly thinking, fight
over a little spring;

and I myself with the spear
among the war-loving Trojans am conspicuous, in that I ward off from them
the day of necessity;

for to you gave
victory Zeus, the son of Cronus, and Apollo, who subdued me
easily;
